Portions derived from FreeFrame (MIT)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Portions of this software are derived from FreeFrame (MIT), commit
`929f5f5306b54958c9c4f11bd1a283c8255eff76` ("2FA part 2 of 2: settings UI,
and two backend gaps found tracing it", 2026-09-19).

FreeFrame's MIT licence, which continues to apply to those portions, is
reproduced in LICENSES/MIT-FreeFrame.txt.

Files were copied from that commit's tracked tree — not forked, and with no
git history. FilmBill is a separate repository; FreeFrame is not a remote of
it, and fixes to shared modules are ported by hand in both directions.

Top-level directories and modules copied, and then trimmed:

  apps/api/
    config.py, database.py, main.py
    middleware/      auth, global_rate_limit, no_cache_errors, rate_limit,
                     setup_guard
    models/          user (incl. the two-factor columns), activity,
                     site_settings, email_settings
    routers/         auth (incl. every /auth/2fa/* endpoint), admin, users,
                     setup, notifications, events, site_settings,
                     email_settings; files.py is derived from FreeFrame's
                     hls_proxy.py with all HLS handling removed
    schemas/         auth, site_settings, email_settings, notification,
                     activity
    services/        auth_service, totp_service, site_settings_service,
                     activity_service, email_service, email_config,
                     event_service, notification_prefs, redis_service,
                     s3_service, secrets_service, schedule_window,
                     permissions
    tasks/           celery_app, email_tasks
    templates/email/ base, invite, magic_code, password_reset_code
    tests/           the suites covering the modules above
    alembic/         env.py and scaffolding only — FreeFrame's migration
                     history was NOT carried over

  apps/web/
    app/(auth)/            login, setup, invite
    app/(dashboard)/       layout shell, notifications, settings (profile,
                           appearance, notifications, branding, admin)
    components/            auth/, layout/, settings/, shared/, ui/
    hooks/, lib/, stores/  the ones the pages above use
    design tokens          inlined into app/globals.css from FreeFrame's
                           packages/design-tokens

  root
    docker-compose.dev.yml, docker-compose.prod.yml, .dockerignore,
    .gitignore, .env.example, .github/workflows/ci.yml

Not copied: everything media-related — assets, uploads, the HLS proxy,
transcoding, transcription and Whisper, LUTs, sidecars, metadata, approvals,
votes, comments, folders, FreeFrame projects, share links, zip export, the
purge service, storage limits and prefixes, the contact form, poster and
thumbnail handling, and the desktop app.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party services
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

FilmBill calls Gotenberg (https://gotenberg.dev, MIT) as a separate container
to render HTML to PDF. No Gotenberg code is included in this repository.

Python and JavaScript dependencies keep their own licences; see
apps/api/requirements.txt and apps/web/package.json.
